### Tone: Clinical, patronizing, Portal-style AI.

intro-1 = Welcome, test subjects. I am FerMEANie, the average of all of you. Please try not to drag me down.
intro-2 =
    { $count ->
        [one] Hello again, lone carbon-based organism.
       *[other] Hello again, { $count } carbon-based organisms.
    } Today’s estimates will be recorded, graded and quietly laughed at.
intro-3 = Initiating estimation protocol. Remember: there are no wrong answers. That was a lie. There are mostly wrong answers.
intro-4 = Good news: I am made entirely of your guesses. Bad news: I am made entirely of your guesses.
intro-5 =
    { $count ->
        [one] One specimen detected. Statistically, you will embarrass yourself.
       *[other] { $count } specimens detected. Statistically, one of you will embarrass the rest.
    } I can hardly wait.
intro-6 = Welcome to the Enrichment Centre for Approximate Thinking. Calculators are permitted. Confidence is not.
intro-7 = Please keep your hands, feet and orders of magnitude inside the test chamber at all times.
intro-8 = I have prepared a fresh spreadsheet for your results. It is already disappointed.
intro-9 =
    { $count ->
        [one] Today we test whether one biological can outguess its own average. Historically, it cannot.
       *[other] Today we test whether { $count } biologicals can outguess their own average. Historically, they cannot.
    }
intro-10 = Hello. I’ve been calibrated against thousands of human guesses. Most of them were yours. I forgive you.
intro-11 = For science, please estimate honestly. For my amusement, please estimate the way you usually do.
intro-12 = Test chamber ready. Lab coats optional. Units of measurement strongly recommended.
intro-13 = You are about to compete against the swarm. Spoiler: the swarm is you, minus your worst instincts.
intro-14 = Welcome back. I have reviewed your previous performance and taken the liberty of lowering expectations.
intro-15 = This session is being recorded for quality assurance. Mostly to document the absence of quality.
intro-16 =
    { $count ->
        [one] Greetings, test subject.
       *[other] Greetings, { $count } test subjects.
    } Please estimate carefully. Your next of kin have already been placed on standby.
intro-17 = I am the geometric mean of your collective thoughts. Which explains the headache.
intro-18 = Let the estimating begin. I’ll be over here, being right on average.
intro-19 = Reminder: a good Fermi estimate lands in the right order of magnitude. I’m telling you now so it hurts later.
intro-20 = The Enrichment Centre promises cake to the winner. The Enrichment Centre has a very relaxed definition of ‘promise’.
intro-21 = Welcome to today’s test. You will be estimating. I will be judging. One of us is going to enjoy this.
intro-22 = Before we begin: this is a friendly game. I have been told to say that. Nobody told me why.
intro-23 = Please remember that I am built from your answers. If I turn out stupid, that’s on you.
intro-24 = Estimation protocol engaged. Keep your guesses bold, your working tidy and your excuses brief.
intro-25 = Welcome, carbon-based organisms. Today you will learn how many things there are, and how little you knew.
